## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical understanding of retrieval pipelines using chunking, embeddings, and vector stores, along with knowledge of real-world metrics for evaluating RAG systems.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)
- Document chunking strategies (size, overlap, and trade-offs)
- Embedding models and vector stores
- Two-stage retrieval (dense retrieval + reranking)
- Evaluation metrics: recall@K and latency benchmarks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal chunking sketch (size=512, overlap=128)
function chunkText(text, size = 512, overlap = 128) {
  const chunks = [];
  let start = 0;
  while (start < text.length) {
    const end = start + size;
    chunks.push(text.slice(start, end));
    start += size - overlap;
  }
  return chunks;
}

// Two-step retrieval call
async function retrieve(query, topK = 10) {
  const queryEmbedding = await embedModel.embed(query);
  const initialResults = await vectorStore.search(queryEmbedding, topK * 3);
  const reranked = await reranker.rerank(query, initialResults, topK);
  return reranked;
}
```

